    {
      "statement_id": "physics.thermodynamics.gibbs_entropy",
      "title": "Gibbs Entropy (Boltzmann-Gibbs Statistical Entropy)",
      "statement_class": "definition",
      "epistemic_status": "formal",
      "theory_context": {
        "disciplines": [
          "physics"
        ],
        "subfield": "thermodynamics",
        "topic": "statistical_mechanics"
      },
      "formal_statement": {
        "canonical_ascii": "S = -(kB * sum_i p_i*ln(p_i))",
        "canonical_latex": "S = -k_B \\sum_i p_i \\ln p_i",
        "equivalent_forms": [
          {
            "form_id": "boltzmann",
            "notation_system": "ascii",
            "expression": "S = kB*ln(W)",
            "scope_note": "Boltzmann's form for W equally likely microstates; the uniform special case"
          },
          {
            "form_id": "von_neumann",
            "notation_system": "measure_theoretic",
            "expression": "S = -kB*Tr(rho*ln(rho))",
            "scope_note": "Quantum form; reduces to the Gibbs sum in the eigenbasis of the density matrix"
          },
          {
            "form_id": "canonical_ensemble",
            "notation_system": "ascii",
            "expression": "S = (U - F)/T",
            "scope_note": "Thermodynamic identity recovered when the p_i are the Boltzmann weights"
          },
          {
            "form_id": "shannon_units",
            "notation_system": "ascii",
            "expression": "S = kB * ln(2) * H(X)",
            "scope_note": "Conversion to bits; the whole content of the information-theory twin"
          }
        ]
      },
      "structural_signature": {
        "archetype_id": "negated_scaled_expected_log",
        "anonymized_template": "ENTROPY = -(SCALE * sum_i PROBABILITY_i * LOG(PROBABILITY_i))",
        "slot_schema": [
          {
            "slot_id": "ENTROPY",
            "syntactic_category": "variable",
            "semantic_role": "output"
          },
          {
            "slot_id": "SCALE",
            "syntactic_category": "constant",
            "semantic_role": "unit_scale_constant"
          },
          {
            "slot_id": "PROBABILITY_i",
            "syntactic_category": "variable",
            "semantic_role": "distribution_weight"
          }
        ],
        "invariants": [
          "The microstate-probability slot occurs twice inside the summand -- as the weight and inside the logarithm -- which is what makes the quantity an expected log-probability rather than a sum of independent contributions.",
          "kB is a fixed constant, not a fitted parameter: it converts between the dimensionless count of states and thermodynamic units of J/K, and occupies the same parameter-like slot that information theory fills with 1/ln 2.",
          "Extensive: for independent subsystems the joint distribution factors and the entropies add, which is the property the logarithm is there to supply.",
          "Maximized, at fixed constraints, by the distribution that maximizes it subject to those constraints -- the canonical ensemble is that maximizer under fixed mean energy, which is Jaynes' derivation.",
          "Zero for a pure state (a single microstate with probability 1), the third-law reference point."
        ]
      },
      "symbol_lexicon": {
        "symbols": [
          {
            "symbol": "S",
            "syntactic_category": "variable",
            "semantic_role": "output",
            "mathematical_order": 0,
            "description": "Statistical (Gibbs) entropy of the ensemble."
          },
          {
            "symbol": "p_i",
            "syntactic_category": "distribution",
            "semantic_role": "distribution_weight",
            "mathematical_order": 0,
            "description": "Probability of microstate i in the ensemble."
          },
          {
            "symbol": "T",
            "syntactic_category": "variable",
            "semantic_role": "state_variable",
            "mathematical_order": 0,
            "description": "Absolute temperature, which converts entropy to energy in the thermodynamic identities."
          }
        ],
        "operators": [
          {
            "symbol": "=",
            "name": "equality",
            "arity": 2,
            "operator_family": "relational"
          },
          {
            "symbol": "*",
            "name": "multiplication",
            "arity": 2,
            "operator_family": "arithmetic"
          },
          {
            "symbol": "-",
            "name": "negation",
            "arity": 1,
            "operator_family": "arithmetic"
          },
          {
            "symbol": "sum",
            "name": "summation over microstates",
            "arity": 1,
            "operator_family": "arithmetic"
          }
        ],
        "functionals": [
          {
            "notation": "LOG(.)",
            "name": "logarithm",
            "input_arity": 1,
            "codomain": "extended reals",
            "description": "Logarithm of a positive argument; natural log in the thermodynamic convention. The base is absorbed into the scale constant, which is why that constant is an explicit slot here."
          }
        ],
        "index_sets": [
          {
            "notation": "i in Omega",
            "domain": "the set of accessible microstates",
            "description": "Index running over the microstates of the ensemble."
          }
        ],
        "constants": [
          {
            "symbol": "kB",
            "value": 1.380649e-23,
            "description": "Boltzmann constant in J/K. Fixes the units of entropy; the information-theoretic reading replaces it by 1/ln 2 to count bits, and Landauer's bound kB*T*ln 2 is the exchange rate between the two."
          }
        ]
      },
      "semantic_interpretation": {
        "statement_meaning": "The entropy of an ensemble is the negated, kB-scaled average of the logarithm of its own microstate probabilities.",
        "statistical_significance": "The corpus's information/thermodynamics bridge, and the node added specifically to test whether the twin thesis survives contact with a case where the identity is claimed to be literal rather than analogical. It does: the typed skeleton `?0:V = neg(*(?1:P, sum⟨*(?2:V, LOG⟨?2:V⟩)⟩))` is shared character for character with infotheory.entropy.shannon_entropy, and the two templates are authored identically modulo slot names because the underlying claim -- Shannon's, sharpened by Jaynes and priced by Landauer -- is that thermodynamic entropy *is* missing information about the microstate, in units of kB instead of bits. The reciprocal `equivalent_to` edge between the two nodes is therefore meant literally, with the base-conversion constant as the exchange rate. Within physics the node also supplies the statistical foundation the chemistry corpus's Gibbs free energy leans on: the ENTROPY slot in `FREE_ENERGY = ENTHALPY - TEMPERATURE * ENTROPY` is this quantity.",
        "regularity_conditions": [
          "A well-defined ensemble with normalized microstate probabilities",
          "Terms with p_i = 0 read as 0 via the limit x*ln(x) -> 0",
          "Discrete (or suitably coarse-grained) microstates; the continuous phase-space version needs a reference measure to be well defined"
        ],
        "failure_modes": [
          "For continuous phase spaces the sum becomes an integral that is not invariant under change of variables; a reference measure (h^3N per cell) must be supplied, which is where the classical entropy's additive constant and the Gibbs paradox come from.",
          "Gibbs entropy of an isolated system under Hamiltonian evolution is constant, so the second law needs coarse-graining or an open system; deriving increase from this formula alone is circular.",
          "Reading kB as a free parameter invites nonsense: it is a fixed conversion factor, and since the 2019 SI redefinition it is exact."
        ]
      },
